• Restart=: Tells systemd when to auto-revive the app. always means systemd will restart it if it crashes, gets killed, or exits cleanly.

• RestartSec=: How long systemd should wait before attempting a restart.


3. The [Install] Section

This section dictates when the service(.service file) should activate relative to the system's boot cycle, used when you type systemctl to enable this service.
• WantedBy=: Links this service to a specific milestone target. multi-user.target is the standard target for a normal, non-graphical terminal environment (similar to Runlevel 3 in old SysV init). When you enable the service, it hooks into this target so it boots automatically on startup.

